From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 23:54:44 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wsi/metal: an opaque swap chain's layer is opaque on iOS

For a hardware device the Metal WSI sets the layer's opaque to NO even
when the swap chain asks for opaque composition, to work around a
Metal 4 presentation bug. On iOS a layer that is not opaque is always
composited (the Metal HUD reads Composited, not Direct): Hollow Knight
under DXVK ran at 80 fps on a 120 Hz panel with 6.7 ms of GPU time.
With the layer opaque it presents correctly, the HUD reads Direct and
the game runs at 119 fps. Keep the workaround off iOS.

Class: ios-port
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-09-26-vulkan-d3d11-d3d12.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
 src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common_metal.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common_metal.c b/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common_metal.c
index 50bac21..049cde2 100644
--- a/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common_metal.c
+++ b/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common_metal.c
@@ -954,7 +954,15 @@ wsi_metal_surface_create_swapchain(VkIcdSurfaceBase *icd_surface,
     * be blitting to the drawable, which means rendering, we can
     * set the framebuffer only usage.
     */
+#if TARGET_OS_IPHONE
+   /* On iOS an opaque layer presents fine through Metal 4, and a layer that
+    * is not opaque is always composited: the display cannot scan it out
+    * directly (Metal HUD: "Composited" rather than "Direct"), which costs a
+    * compositor pass and a frame of latency on every present. */
+   const bool layer_opaque = opaque_composition;
+#else
    const bool layer_opaque = opaque_composition && wsi_device->sw;
+#endif
    const bool framebuffer_only = !wsi_device->sw;
 
    VkResult result = wsi_metal_layer_configure(metal_surface->pLayer,
